    "description": "<h2>Summary</h2><p>Set the final Deal Status value list once so lifecycle stories consume a single field definition.</p><h2>Final values</h2><table><thead><tr><th><p>Order</p></th><th><p>API value</p></th><th><p>Label</p></th><th><p>Meaning</p></th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Draft</p></td><td><p>Draft</p></td><td><p>Being set up; default; never sent to CMS.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>2</p></td><td><p>Active</p></td><td><p>Active</p></td><td><p>Salesforce has activated/intends the Deal to be live. CMS Sync Status separately shows whether CMS accepted the latest state.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>3</p></td><td><p>Paused</p></td><td><p>Paused</p></td><td><p>Temporary operational pause; lifecycle action hides/deactivates active Links and can later restore the pre-pause active set.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>4</p></td><td><p>Inactive</p></td><td><p>Inactive</p></td><td><p>Automated informational state after inactivity threshold; does not deactivate Links or alter DRAs.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>5</p></td><td><p>Closed</p></td><td><p>Closed</p></td><td><p>Longer-term locked state; reactivatable by permitted users.</p></td></tr><tr><td><p>6</p></td><td><p>Archived</p></td><td><p>Archived</p></td><td><p>Terminal; never normally reactivated; releases makeup.</p></td></tr></tbody></table><p>Deactivate Review Required rather than delete it.</p><h2>Requirements</h2><ul><li><p>Keep restricted picklist and field history.</p></li><li><p>Set Draft as default.</p></li><li><p>API values are exactly Draft, Active, Paused, Inactive, Closed, Archived.</p></li><li><p>Verify the actual deployed metadata uses <strong>Archived</strong> spelling.</p></li><li><p>Review Required is inactive and cannot be newly set through normal UI/API.</p></li><li><p>This story defines values only; behavior belongs to lifecycle action stories.</p></li></ul><h2>Important semantic clarification</h2><ul><li><p><strong>Active does not mean CMS sync succeeded.</strong> Active may coexist with CMS Sync Status = Failed/Retrying.</p></li><li><p><strong>Inactive is informational only.</strong> CMS must not interpret it as Pause/hide Links merely because the status value is Inactive.</p></li></ul><h2>Out of scope</h2><ul><li><p>Archive action/makeup release.</p></li><li><p>Closed locking/reactivation behavior.</p></li><li><p>Pause Link-state restoration.</p></li><li><p>CMS contract implementation.</p></li></ul>",
